    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9712ccf1_7337859b",
        "filename": "common/ap_hang_detect.c",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 115,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-05T13:37:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If the expected API contract is that the host sends SET_PARAM and then RELOAD before the watchdog starts, I think `hang_detect_cancel()` on any SET_PARAM makes sense.\n\nThe alternative is that SET_PARAM calls `hang_detect_reload()` to automatically arm the watchdog.  Then RELOAD is only used to pet the watchdog.",
      "parentUuid": "3466e437_417b6b3c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 115,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 115,
        "endChar": 23
      },
      "revId": "9b3a3a51821a526eefd46ce6f8bc79f5f777c5b8",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cd6d9afd_66cb587a",
        "filename": "common/ap_hang_detect.c",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 115,
      "author": {
        "id": 1442602
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-05T13:47:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I have dig deeper also on the kernel code and there is no need to care about this use case, as when setting the new timeout, kernel immediately pets the watchdog (so in turn calls the `hang_detect_reload()` in the end):\nreference:\nhttps://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel/+/refs/heads/chromeos-6.6/drivers/watchdog/watchdog_dev.c#804\n\nupdate: ayyyyy it looks I forgot to sent this comment before sending the CL.",
      "parentUuid": "3466e437_417b6b3c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 115,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 115,
        "endChar": 23
      },
      "revId": "9b3a3a51821a526eefd46ce6f8bc79f5f777c5b8",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8f4f8a86_9a9ad992",
        "filename": "common/ap_hang_detect.c",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 115,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-12T16:59:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If the kernel always does the pet right after SET_TIMEOUT, then a `hang_detect_cancel()` makes sense here.\n\nThat way the AP hang detect state has only 3 possible states:\n* At init time or after CANCEL: no timeout set, watchdog not running\n* After SET_TIMEOUT: timeout is set, watchdog not running\n* After RELOAD: watchdog running (if timeout set)\n\nOtherwise the state after SET_TIMEOUT differs based on whether the AP previously did a RELOAD.\n\nThis contract should be detailed in ec_commands.h.",
      "parentUuid": "cd6d9afd_66cb587a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 115,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 115,
        "endChar": 23
      },
